{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":287220,"name":"Peter Bierma","username":"ZeroIntensity","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/zerointensity/{size}/10639_2.png","created_at":"2026-03-08T03:51:29.438Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m proposing a few new changes to support \u003ccode\u003eyield from\u003c/code\u003e in asynchronous generators. Namely:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAllowing an asynchronous generator to use \u003ccode\u003eyield from\u003c/code\u003e to delegate to a synchronous subgenerator.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdding an \u003ccode\u003easync yield from\u003c/code\u003e statement to delegate to an asynchronous subgenerator.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAllowing non-\u003ccode\u003eNone\u003c/code\u003e return values in asynchronous generators for when \u003ccode\u003easync yield from\u003c/code\u003e is an expression.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere’s an example to visualize:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"py\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-py\"\u003edef sync_generator():\n    yield 1\n\nasync def async_generator():\n    yield 2\n    return 3\n\nasync def main():\n    yield from sync_generator()\n    result = async yield from async_generator()\n    assert result == 3\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVariations of this idea have come up on here a few times before. The main pushback I’ve seen is that the implementation would be too complex. Following some of my own frustration with a lack of support for \u003ccode\u003eyield from\u003c/code\u003e in async generators, I was able to come up with a \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/python/cpython/compare/main...zerointensity:cpython:async-yield-from\"\u003ereference implementation\u003c/a\u003e that isn’t particularly maintenance-heavy. (The majority of the diff comes from the regenerated parser and interpreter.)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI have a \u003ca href=\"https://pep-previews--4854.org.readthedocs.build/pep-0828/\"\u003ePEP draft\u003c/a\u003e on this; I suggest reading that for more details.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-03-08T22:39:46.731Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":113,"reads":140,"readers_count":139,"score":773.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":106430,"topic_slug":"supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators","display_username":"Peter Bierma","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/python/cpython/compare/main...zerointensity:cpython:async-yield-from","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Comparing python:main...zerointensity:async-yield-from · python/cpython · GitHub","clicks":8},{"url":"https://pep-previews--4854.org.readthedocs.build/pep-0828/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 828 – Supporting ‘yield from’ in asynchronous generators | peps.python.org","clicks":4}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":12}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":10246,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators/106430/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":12}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":12,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":287224,"name":"Hayden Welch","username":"hwelch","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/hwelch/{size}/33920_2.png","created_at":"2026-03-08T07:00:01.443Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eAnything that brings async and sync syntax close together has my support. The lack of \u003ccode\u003eyield from\u003c/code\u003e for async code has always been one of those little annoyances that forces me to stop and think for a second.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf this does get added, I’m sure there will be a lot of people who just end up using it accidentally without knowing about this pep since \u003ccode\u003eyield from\u003c/code\u003e is such a common pattern.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-03-08T07:00:01.443Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":120,"readers_count":119,"score":69.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":106430,"topic_slug":"supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators","display_username":"Hayden Welch","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":51399,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators/106430/2","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":287227,"name":"Michael H","username":"mikeshardmind","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/mikeshardmind/{size}/14381_2.png","created_at":"2026-03-08T07:24:23.340Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI’m not fully sold on a specific need for capturing return values with async generators\u003csup class=\"footnote-ref\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#footnote-287227-1\" id=\"footnote-ref-287227-1\"\u003e[1]\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e, but behaviorally, this is what I would expect out of full parity here, and there’s a hard to quantify benefit to improving consistency when it comes to people learning and teaching, as well as writing, reading, and maintaining code to not have to spend an extra moment thinking “is this allowed here?”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis may be a good time for those interested in the type system to re-evaluate how \u003ccode\u003eaync def\u003c/code\u003e is handled in type stubs, as the preexisting issue here where typecheckers rely on being able to see the function body to determine the type of functions defined with \u003ccode\u003easync def\u003c/code\u003e is going to become a larger problem. (Not something I would expect as a blocker to for this)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr class=\"footnotes-sep\"\u003e\n\n\u003col class=\"footnotes-list\"\u003e\n\u003cli id=\"footnote-287227-1\" class=\"footnote-item\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eI’m sure someone can find a reasonable use for it, but I’ve found it generally better to handle code that looks like it would want that with a context manager + an async iterator, or just with synchronous generators. \u003ca href=\"#footnote-ref-287227-1\" class=\"footnote-backref\"\u003e↩︎\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-03-08T07:25:01.394Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":116,"readers_count":115,"score":38.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":106430,"topic_slug":"supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators","display_username":"Michael H","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":15730,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators/106430/3","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":287229,"name":"Monarch","username":"Monarch","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/monarch/{size}/18530_2.png","created_at":"2026-03-08T07:43:12.070Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eYes please. Everytime I’ve encountered this I’ve been annoyed. The spelling is also as natural as it gets and something I’ve reached out to accidentally only to be disappointed. Thank you for working on this.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-03-08T07:43:12.070Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":109,"readers_count":108,"score":36.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":106430,"topic_slug":"supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators","display_username":"Monarch","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":21724,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators/106430/4","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":287232,"name":"Serhiy Storchaka","username":"storchaka","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/storchaka/{size}/217_2.png","created_at":"2026-03-08T08:46:09.721Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eWhy do you need \u003ccode\u003easync yield from\u003c/code\u003e? Do you really write the code like the following (this is a very simplified example) all the time?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"python\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-python\"\u003ewhile True:\n    try:\n        y = yield x\n    except StopAsyncIteration:\n        break\n    except Exception as e:\n        await a.athrow(e)\n        break\n    else:\n        x = await a.asend(y)\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOr you simply want to write\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"python\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-python\"\u003easync for x in a: yield x\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ein one line?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-03-08T08:46:09.721Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":109,"readers_count":108,"score":56.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":106430,"topic_slug":"supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators","display_username":"Serhiy Storchaka","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":44,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators/106430/5","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":287235,"name":"Chris Angelico","username":"Rosuav","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/rosuav/{size}/3429_2.png","created_at":"2026-03-08T08:58:28.394Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI’ve never come across this in actual usage, but orthogonality does have its appeal. +0.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-03-08T08:58:28.394Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":102,"readers_count":101,"score":40.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":106430,"topic_slug":"supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators","display_username":"Chris Angelico","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":3377,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators/106430/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":287258,"name":"Peter Bierma","username":"ZeroIntensity","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/zerointensity/{size}/10639_2.png","created_at":"2026-03-08T15:00:21.978Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote group-committers\" data-username=\"storchaka\" data-display-name=\"Serhiy Storchaka\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"106430\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/storchaka/48/217_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Serhiy Storchaka:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOr you simply want to write\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"python\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-python\"\u003easync for x in a: yield x\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ein one line?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes, that’s the primary use case, and I think the same is true for \u003ccode\u003eyield from\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe issue is that a loop isn’t equivalent to \u003ccode\u003easync yield from\u003c/code\u003e, because subgenerator delegation semantics are lost. That’s the whole reason \u003ccode\u003eyield from\u003c/code\u003e was added in the first place.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-03-08T15:00:21.978Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":96,"readers_count":95,"score":64.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":106430,"topic_slug":"supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators","display_username":"Peter Bierma","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":10246,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators/106430/7","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":287309,"name":"Hayden Welch","username":"hwelch","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/hwelch/{size}/33920_2.png","created_at":"2026-03-09T00:31:40.489Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI’ve run into it a few times when batching things like requests:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"python\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-python\"\u003eimport asyncio\nfrom itertools import batched\n\n# Something that handles a number of request futures\nasync def dispatch_requests(*requests):\n    ...\n\n# The thing that I always reach for before remembering you can't\n# yield from an async generator \nasync def batch_requests(*requests, batch_size):\n    for batch in batched(requests, batch_size):\n        yield from dispatch_requests(*batch)\n\n# The way I end up writing it\nasync def old_batch_requests(*requests, batch_size):\n    for batch in batched(requests, batch_size):\n        async for resp in dispatch_requests(*batch):\n            yield await resp\n\nasync def main():\n    return await asyncio.gather(\n        *batch_requests(..., 10), \n        return_exceptions=True\n    )\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI also do not use async code that often, so this toy example probably has some problems in it, but that sort of pattern is something I’ve run into a lot. Especially since a lot of my sync code is reliant on chains of generators that all \u003ccode\u003eyield from\u003c/code\u003e one another to form data pipelines.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-03-09T00:31:40.489Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":99,"readers_count":98,"score":94.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":106430,"topic_slug":"supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators","display_username":"Hayden Welch","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":3377,"username":"Rosuav","name":"Chris Angelico","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/rosuav/{size}/3429_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":4}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":51399,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/supporting-yield-from-in-asynchronous-generators/106430/8","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":4}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":4,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":287378,"name":"Bartosz Sławecki","username":"bswck","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/bswck/{size}/34363_2.png","created_at":"2026-03-09T19:49:31.836Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003ePEP discussion thread is now open: \u003ca href=\"https://discu